---
import { url } from '../lib/url';
---
<section id="what" aria-labelledby="what-heading">
  <div class="start"><div><h2 id="what-heading">Start with SWE.</h2><p>Kerby provides the engine. SWE supplies the method for coding tasks.</p></div><a class="cta" href={url('rulebooks/swe/')}>Read the SWE guide <span class="direction-arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div>
  <details><summary>Other rulebooks and authoring</summary><p>Kerby loads a selected rulebook into your agent’s session. Each rulebook supplies instructions and declares checks.</p><h3>Skill authoring</h3><p>Instructions that require a fresh evaluation of the exact skill text before presenting it as verified. Guide coming · <a href="https://github.com/sorawit-w/kerby/tree/main/skills/kerby/rulebooks/skill-authoring">Read the source ↗</a></p><p>Have a different kind of work? <a href="https://github.com/sorawit-w/kerby/blob/main/docs/AUTHORING-RULEBOOKS.md">Write a rulebook →</a></p></details>
</section>
<style>
section { border-top:1px solid var(--border); padding-block:2rem; }
.start { display:flex; justify-content:space-between; align-items:center; gap:2rem; }
h2 { margin:0 0 .4rem; font-size:2rem; letter-spacing:-.035em; }
p { margin:.4rem 0 0; color:var(--secondary); }
details { margin-top:1.5rem; font-size:.9rem; }
summary { color:var(--muted); cursor:pointer; }
h3 { margin:1rem 0 .4rem; }
details p + p { margin-top:1rem; }
@media(max-width:600px) { .start { align-items:flex-start; flex-direction:column; gap:1rem; } }
</style>
